  "question": {
    "text": "The curve passing through <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is such that for a tangent drawn to it at a point <math><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the ratio of the&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi></math>-intercept and the ordinate of <math><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then, the equation of the curve is"
  },
